  "id": "exploratory-factor-analysis",
  "term": "exploratory factor analysis",
  "definition": "Exploratory factor analysis is a method used in psychometric assessment to examine a scale’s internal structure and see how its items group into underlying factors. It is often used in early evaluation of a measure to identify the factor pattern before confirming it in a separate sample.",
