      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s claim that exploratory factor analysis is “often used in early evaluation of a measure to identify the factor pattern before confirming it in a separate sample” is not directly supported by the provided packet text. While the packet says EFA and CFA were performed in independent samples, it does not state (in general terms) that EFA is often used specifically to identify a pattern prior to later confirmation.",
        "The packet provides evidence for EFA/CFA being used to evaluate internal structure and support a three-factor structure in a specific adaptation/validation study, but it does not substantiate the broader “often used in early evaluation” phrasing as a general description of the method."
